== test: gh544-pre-push-gate ==
  PASS: a red gate refuses the push (exit 1)
  PASS:   and says the push was REFUSED
  PASS:   and names the escape hatch rather than leaving you stuck
  PASS:   and does not excuse the red merely because hosted CI exists
  PASS: a green gate allows the push (exit 0)
  PASS:   and reports the wall-clock it cost
  PASS:   and announced the mode before running
  PASS: a docs-only push is allowed even when validate.sh is red
  PASS:   and runs the deterministic documentation gate
  PASS:   and does NOT run validate.sh
  PASS: a red documentation gate still refuses the docs-only push
  PASS:   and names the documentation gate failure
  PASS: a code change remains on the full gate
  PASS:   and does NOT take the documentation route
  PASS: an hq push with NO runnable suite falls back to the FULL gate
  PASS:   and validate.sh was NOT asked for a narrow --paths-file run
  PASS: an hq push with its suite present runs the tier 2 gate
  PASS:   and validate.sh received the paths file (the hook's only narrow invocation)
  PASS:   and the gate really ran
  PASS: a RED tier 2 gate still refuses the utility push (exit 1)
  PASS:   and names the tier 2 gate in the refusal
  PASS: the FIRST push of a new branch with a verifiable base runs the tier 2 gate (GH-487)
  PASS:   and validate.sh received the paths file (the shared narrow invocation)
  PASS:   and the narrow gate really ran
  PASS: a new branch with NO origin/development base evidence falls back to the full gate (GH-487)
  PASS: a new branch with NO common ancestor to the integration branch fails closed to full (GH-487)
  PASS: a base equal to the pushed SHA (empty range) fails closed to full (GH-487)
  PASS: a push by URL has no configured remote name and takes the full gate (GH-487)
  PASS:   and says WHY instead of leaving the slowness unexplained
  PASS: a MIXED new-branch + integration-ref push still selects the narrow gate (GH-487)
  PASS:   and validate.sh received the paths file
  PASS: an EMPTY stdin still announces the full gate (nothing narrow can run on no input, GH-487)
  PASS: a BACKWARD-rewritten integration branch fails closed to full (GH-487 round 1)
  PASS: a STALE-BEHIND integration branch (fetch needed) fails closed to full (GH-487 round 1)
  PASS: a FAILED ls-remote (partial ref emitted) fails closed to full (GH-487 round 3)
  PASS:   and names the offline bypass levers (GH-496)
error: unknown option `push'
usage: git ls-remote [--branches] [--tags] [--refs] [--upload-pack=<exec>]
                     [-q | --quiet] [--exit-code] [--get-url] [--sort=<key>]
                     [--symref] [<repository> [<patterns>...]]

    -q, --[no-]quiet      do not print remote URL
    --[no-]upload-pack <exec>
                          path of git-upload-pack on the remote host
    -t, --[no-]tags       limit to tags
    -b, --[no-]branches   limit to branches
    --[no-]refs           do not show peeled tags
    --[no-]get-url        take url.<base>.insteadOf into account
    --[no-]sort <key>     field name to sort on
    --[no-]exit-code      exit with exit code 2 if no matching refs are found
    --[no-]symref         show underlying ref in addition to the object pointed by it
    -o, --[no-]server-option <server-specific>
                          option to transmit

  PASS: a pushurl that disagrees with the fetch url fails closed to full (GH-487 CodeRabbit #2)
  PASS: a NO-OP integration ref in a mixed push contributes no paths and keeps the narrow gate (GH-487 pin)
  PASS: an AMBIGUOUS base (multiple best common ancestors) fails closed to full (GH-487 round 1)
  PASS: XYZ_SKIP_PREPUSH=1 lets a RED tree through (exit 0)
  PASS:   and says loudly that nothing was verified
  PASS: a delete-only push skips the gate even when it is red (exit 0)
  PASS:   and says why
  PASS:   and did NOT run the gate
  PASS: a MIXED delete+real push is still gated (exit 1)
  PASS: --check reports NOT INSTALLED on a fresh clone (exit 1)
  PASS:   and warns the clone will push WITHOUT the gate
  PASS: install succeeds (exit 0)
  PASS:   and writes the stub into the git hooks dir, not the tree
  PASS:   and the stub is identifiable as ours
  PASS:   and core.hooksPath is left UNSET (it would override the stub)
  PASS: --check now reports INSTALLED (exit 0)
  PASS: install is idempotent (exit 0 on a second run)
  PASS: install CLEARS a legacy core.hooksPath=githooks (exit 0)
  PASS:   and says why it cleared it (GH-549)
  PASS:   leaving core.hooksPath unset
  PASS:   and did NOT overwrite the in-tree hook it delegates to
  PASS: --check FAILS when a foreign core.hooksPath overrides the stub (exit 1)
  PASS:   and says the stub will not run
  PASS: install REFUSES to clobber a different core.hooksPath (exit 4)
